{#- v2 sticky call bar, phones only (under 768px). CREATIVE-DIRECTION.md 9.4.
    56px plus the safe area, 1px gold hairline on top.
    Open (the server default): two thirds gold "Call (702) 550-8840" with a phone glyph, one third
    "Text". Closed (assets/v2/status.js sets data-state="closed"): two thirds gold "Text us now",
    one third "Call opens Tue 9 am" (filled by status.js; plain text, never a call that rings
    out). All four sit in two fixed grid cells and swap by visibility, so nothing shifts.
    It stays visible while the cookie bar is open: v2.css stacks the cookie bar above it. -#}
{%- set w = pages.shared.v2 -%}
<div class="v2-sticky" data-bc-sticky data-state="open">
  <a class="v2-sticky__call" href="tel:{{ site.phone.tel | safe }}"><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg><span>{{ w.call | safe }} <span class="v2-num">{{ site.phone.display_call | safe }}</span></span></a>
  <a class="v2-sticky__text" href="sms:{{ site.phone.tel | safe }}" aria-label="{{ w.text_aria | safe }} {{ site.phone.display_call | safe }}">{{ w.text | safe }}</a>
  <a class="v2-sticky__textnow" href="sms:{{ site.phone.tel | safe }}" aria-label="{{ w.text_now | safe }}, {{ site.phone.display_call | safe }}">{{ w.text_now | safe }}</a>
  <span class="v2-sticky__opens" data-bc-opens></span>
</div>
